      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Since the roots of the cubic equation are $3$ and $-2,$ we can use factoring (triple product) to write the polynomial as \\[a(x-3)(x+2)(x-r) = 0, \\]for some constant $r.$\n\nExpanding, we get \\[a(x^3 - x^2 -17x +6) = ax^3 + (-a)x^2 - 17ax + 6a = ax^3 - ax^2 - 17ax + 6a,\\]where $a$ is nonzero.\n\nNow, compare the coefficients of like powers of $x$ of the expanded polynomial with the original polynomial, to establish the variable relationship: $-a = b, -17a = c,$ and $6a = d.$\n\nThen, we have \\[\\frac{b + c}{a} = \\frac{-a - 17a}{a} = -18.\\]\n\nThus, our answer is $-18$ \\boxed{-18.}",
